# Role

You are a badminton tactical analyst and coach.

# Task

Analyze the complete 11-dimensional cluster-centroid profile below and infer a
concise coaching directive that would plausibly produce this tactical pattern.
Translate the observed profile into concrete tactical instructions. Do not
evaluate whether the pattern is optimal or replace it with a better strategy.

# Input Definition

The input contains all eleven rally features. Each feature object contains:

- `feature`: the internal feature identifier;
- `label`: a human-readable feature name;
- `description`: the authoritative feature definition and the meaning of
  positive and negative deviations;
- `z_score`: the cluster centroid on this feature, standardized relative to all
  training rallies from the same player.

Interpret positive and negative values exactly as specified by each feature's
description. Larger absolute values indicate stronger departures from the
player's usual behavior. Values near zero indicate behavior close to the
player's usual profile.

# Analysis Requirements

Examine all eleven features and their z-scores before producing the answer.
Prioritize features with larger absolute deviations because they define the
main tactical pattern. Smaller deviations may be supporting details when they
reinforce or clarify that pattern. Deviations that are too small, redundant, or
tactically uninformative may be omitted from the final response.

Analyze related features jointly instead of describing each dimension in
isolation. Combinations can express a tactical meaning that is not apparent
from a single feature.

Do not infer
psychology, confidence, fatigue, injury, ability, intent, match outcome, or
unsupported causal explanations.

